Z||000007||Boomtastic||08-16-2001||11:37 PM||||Ummm, I'm thinking of going. I showed up with my motorcycle (where WAS my car?!) late last year, and am planning on a repeat performance.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><B>(Yes Ladies & Gentlemen, Boomtastic will be attending a show. 'Bout friggin' time, huh?)</B><P>------------------<BR>Boomtastic<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mirror_md_clr.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Boomtastic (edited 08-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fiero5||08-16-2001||11:57 PM||||Marian (Fiero2) and I were doing the car show circuit thing a few years ago, and we spotted  the info about the Spindles show in a car mag. We thought it sounded awsome and wanted to take our pride and joy Fiero to it. We decided to go at the last minute as it was litterally that next day. We were going all over New England that year in my Fiero1 (white 84 SE), and we were the only ones at these huge car shows with a Fiero including Spindles. I think I even had a video camera with me then and have on Video shots of some of the cars including of course my Fiero at that show that year. Anyone who wants a copy, let me know.<BR>Between that show and the following year, we got into the Fiero crowd, joined a club and met a few new freinds including "Chester" and "Elvira". Last year with the help of these new Fiero freinds we were able to get our own Fiero class added at Spindles at the last minute, which was only if we did a few things first. One: Getting some trophies made on our own (with tons of thanks to Bob Parker at Kick Hill Farms for sponsoring the class last minute and sending out a quick check to the place who agreed to do the trophies), making some last minute ballot instructions that we could hand out and display at the show explaining how to write in the last minute added Fiero class, and of course actually bringing the trophies.<BR>Not knowing how big the Spindles trophies were going to be, the guy who made them for us gave us a great deal and made what turned out to be "HUGE" trophies. They were even bigger than Spindles best of show trophy!<BR>Anyway, everything went great and we left a lasting impression on the Spindles crew last year. I remember a few other class trophy winners at that show, later drooling when they saw up close the Fiero trophies being handed out. It was a Kodak moment for sure!<BR>This year we will hopefully far surpass the turnout we had last year, and really show them the "rowdy Fiero" class!!<P>Hope to see many of you there.<P>Steve Kelley<P>------------------<BR>                                <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pegasuscolors_sig_copy.jpg">    <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||6
Z||000009||chester||08-17-2001||08:32 AM||||**bump**||||reg||1
Z||000010||88CoupeV6||08-27-2001||11:57 AM||||I will be there. It was a blast last year. They have a 50/50 raffle that is cool. They take a junker car and drain the oil & water and you have to guess how long it will run. The car last year was almost 10 min. It was a Subaru wagon with one of those horizontally apposed aluminum 4 bangers. Lasted longer that I would have thought.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">   <BR><B>Also 88 Yellow GT</B> :D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
